#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# log_normal_distribution

#% text
# `log_normal_distribution(mu, sigma)` is the distribution of `exp(X)` for `X` normal with mean `mu` and standard deviation `sigma > 0`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mean(log_normal_distribution(mu, sigma))
#% output
#= exp(mu + (1/2)*sigma^2)

#% cell
pdf(log_normal_distribution(0, 1), 1.0)
#% output
#= 0.3989422804014327

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The median is `exp(mu)`:

#% cell
n(quantile(log_normal_distribution(1, 1/2), 1/2))
#% output
#= 2.718281828459045

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `normal_distribution`, `quantile`, `pdf`
